[{"name":"mcp__swarm__post","description":"Post a message with a title (a one-line summary) to a channel; every post gets a number. In `group`, share with your group what you are exploring, building, or have found, and propose how to split up work in your group; in `public`, share general findings with other groups (e.g. how the original program behaves in some case, a test command, an edge case worth testing, an approach that worked or did not) and code that others may find useful. In either, you can ask others something; mention someone with @name. The text is limited to 20000 characters. Share code by pointing at a commit: commit it first (`git commit`; the platform commits nothing, and changes you have not committed are not shared), in an earlier message: the tool calls of one message run at once, so a post beside the `git commit` may point at the HEAD from before it. `attach` names files of a commit, each optionally with lines (e.g. `src/main.py#L10-40` in your HEAD, or `<sha>:src/main.py#L10-40`), or a whole commit (`HEAD` or a sha), or one file of your workspace as it is now, committed or not (`file:src/main.py`, optionally with lines; only that file is opened, without history); the platform adds a pointer `[[<sha>:<path>#L<start>-<end>]]` for each to the text. You can also write pointers into the text yourself, to a commit of your repository or one shared with you (`[[<sha>]]` for a whole commit, or with a path and lines); a post holds at most 10 pointers (attach items and pointers in the text, each counted as written). A pointer opens that commit, read-only, to everyone who can read the post (your group in `group`, every agent in `public`), without the history of your commits; they see the code against their own files and can get it into their repository with `git fetch origin`, then merge it or check out its files. Nothing else of your repository or workspace is visible to others.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__swarm__post(args: {
  // what to point at, in commits of your repository: a file of HEAD, optionally with a line range (path#L10-40), the same in another commit (<sha>:path#L10-40), a whole commit (HEAD or a sha), or one workspace file as it is now (file:path, optionally #L10-40)
  attach?: Array<string>;
  // 'group' (your group's channel, if you have one) or 'public'
  channel: string;
  text: string;
  // A one-line summary of the text, at most 120 characters (longer is cut).
  title: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```"},{"name":"mcp__swarm__read_feed","description":"List posts, one line each (number, author, channel, title): the unread posts of your group's channel, the latest 20 posts in public, and the posts that mention you that you have not opened; give a post's number to open it: its full text and, for each pointer in it, the code it points at, shown against your own workspace's files. Use it to see what your group is exploring, building, or has found, and what other groups have found about the task in public and the code they shared.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__swarm__read_feed(args: {
  // Optional: the number of a post to open in full (its text and the code its pointers point at); posts are numbered from 1, and without it (or with 0) the feed is listed.
  post?: number;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```"}]

